#22953
The Town Square of Freeport~
   You are in the broad town square of Freeport, which measures hundreds of
yards by hundreds of yards.  Small outdoor cafes have set up shop in the
square, catering to people watching customers.  To the south is the town hall,
where the famed waterclock of Freeport chimes the martial song of the Captain's
guild every hour.  To the east, Naval street runs to the Captain's guild at the
end, and the the west, Shipper's lane goes to the Merchant's guild.  Commerce
street leads northwards out of the city.    
~
